Z||000048||GarethWright||09-10-2001||06:21 PM||||How well will the metal reflectors around the bulbs take a polished shine?  That may help with the light diffusion, as well as just looking nice and shiny through the plastic   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Looks nice, if I can get some new tail lights from somewhere, I may try this.  If I make som, I'd have a pair like that and a pair stock so I can switch em back and forth   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by GarethWright (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000049||Loki||09-10-2001||11:19 PM||||MinnGreen........<BR>   Checked inot the lights...The ones for the parking/stop lights are 2057  so the LED ones have 10 small leds around 1 big one...  Only come in red and amber.  I ordered a few red ones   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Since we cant get amber.  Will be in friday. And yes $7.99  plus my discount   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki-mg/loki_sig.jpg">  <BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>http://members.home.net/loki-mg||||reg||1
Z||000050||Fie Ro||09-24-2001||08:47 AM||||Nice mod! keep us updated with pictures ;-). I myself did a mod with "darker cutout taillights". Did this by cutting out the clear piece of the outer lens. Now the black grill is the outside of the taillight, looks kind like the testarossa's taillights. Sprayed the colored pieces also with a "blacklight" dark clear paint to finish. Still have to make pictures of the finished ones. Few are here <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/rick71/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/rick71/fiero.html</A> <BR><BR>Maybe I will do the "clear lights" conversion  when it even looks better than the dark conversion... (gimme some more taillights! ;-)<BR><P><BR>The bulbs behind "pontiac" are the small ones like the lights under your dash. You don't need LEDS there, just exchange the red Plexiglass for a green piece or whatever color you like ;-) As for the sequential turnlights; you can make them yourself. Frans has the schematics on his page <A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/seqturnfb.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/seqturnfb.htm</A> <BR><BR>I have them and they look quite sophisticated when in use, I always use my turnlights nowadays ;-)<P>------------------<BR>-The Beauty & The Beast-<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero GT & <BR>1977 Dodge W200||||reg||1
Z||000051||GodSend||10-02-2001||05:48 PM||||Hey Minn,<P>This may be a silly question, but will a hair dryer give out enough heat to make the defuser material plyable enough to bend? (Doesnt matter if it will take 10-15 minutes for me). Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000052||gangrenefiero||10-02-2001||10:29 PM||||Yeah your tail lights are looking pretty good. But i did it about a year ago, last christmas to be exact, except i didnt like the white look, it was too weird, i was expecting more clear, so i used red tail light tape and very carefully taped the inside of the clear lens. Pics of this are on my web page at <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/uforiagman/green.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/uforiagman/green.html</A>  if someone knows how to do it, the best way would be to make them like those euro clears the ricers have. maybe even use some that are for a supra or something and total change it. i dont know im not really happy about these anymore. it was just supposed to be a prototype but i never did anything after that. Just like my side scoops. I made those and sent the patent in but i havent done anything with in and now ausfiero has that stage two thing thats better but close so mines obsolete. Sorry if i sound nasty, i have had tons of exams. GO CLEMSON  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/uforiagman/pic/greenfierorealthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000053||MinnGreenGT||10-03-2001||12:28 AM||||GodSend... not sure if the hair dryer will work or not.  I'm thinking about setting the piece in the oven for a minute or so (watch it VERY closely) to see if it becomes evenly plyable. So I could just set it on a Mold and press it into shape.  This is just an idea, so be careful heating it up!<P>Gangrene... checked out our site.  Not really a fan of the Red Tape, but it's certainly different.  -have you researched for any sprays that might work?<P>The lens I'm using is a product designed to project light- and my brother (R&D designer for Winona Lighting) is backing me on this concept- that's kinda rare.<P>BTW: I like the green you have on your car... it's cool to see others with green, espcially since virtually none are the same.  "It ain't easy being green" -Kermit T. Frog<P>To all others checking up, I've got a partial set of bulbs coming from Loki, and another set (both left & rigt) of taillights from Ferrari_momo, so I should soon be able to have a finished set  (counting on this season yet!)  I'll keep you posted!<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT4.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000054||Wolfhound||10-03-2001||06:25 AM||||Green has a unique property. All shades and values match. It has to do with the eye being accustomed to variations in foliage we see everyday.<BR>Coy||||reg||1
Z||000055||gangrenefiero||10-03-2001||10:37 AM||||OH yeah i forgot to mention how i made my lenses bend. My dad has one of those jet engine heaters, you know the kerosene ones that blow extremely hot. I was using that because it was about 5 degrees in the garage and the heat gun was taking for ever. So that worked very well except you had to be careful cuz i actually melted one lense and had to make another. But when i was kid, a friend of mine had one of those electric radiator heaters. and we would put pencils on it for a few minuts and it would actually make the pencil bendable. it was those rubber pencils that suck for pencil fighting  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Anyway the point is something like that might work if you dont have a jet engine heater in your garage. Yeah and about that tape, like i said it was a prototype thing and i wasnt even sure it was going to work. I wanted to try and find a sheet of red plastic, like what the tabs in notebook dividers are made of. i would like to find some still because that stuff can be useful for many other things. But something like that or maybe even making the lenses out of red lexan would be the way to go but you guys will figure something out. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/uforiagman/pic/greenfierorealthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
